Title: Test feasibility of a country-quarter JETP approval comparison
Created: 2026-09-15
Author: HDMX-coding-agent

--- log ---
2026-09-15T00:01Z HDMX-coding-agent created after the author authorised 0729's bounded pre-outcome feasibility screen.
--- body ---

## Context

Ticket 0729 reached a causal DEFER: neither historical project clocks, sector
comparisons nor a country comparison currently has defended identification. The
author has authorised one narrow next step, a design-only feasibility screen for
a possible country-quarter concessional-approval comparison. The screen may
return GO, NARROW or DEFER. It is not an estimator, a causal result, or an
authorisation for 0730 implementation.

## First test (Red)

Write a failing contract test proving that the feasibility-screen loader rejects
any country-quarter observation that lacks a source version and locator, approval
date semantics, currency basis, concessionality/instrument rule, or an explicit
missingness and denominator/lost-visibility state. The test must also reject a
country marked as untreated when its negotiation-exposure field is unknown.
Only then implement the smallest loader/validator needed to make it pass.

## Scope and protocol

Freeze before looking at treated-minus-comparison outcomes:

1. Candidate-country universe with inclusion/exclusion reasons; JETP and
   negotiation exposure; income, financing eligibility, coal/power context;
   shared lenders; and concurrent policy, debt, election, crisis and finance
   interventions.
2. Treatment calendar retaining distinct negotiation, declaration, plan,
   operational/facility and first-approval dates, with sources and defensible
   alternatives. Do not substitute an announcement date silently.
3. Country-quarter approval contract retaining source version/locator, lender,
   instrument, concessionality rule, currency basis, status, identifiers, date
   precision, missingness, lost visibility and historical-denominator state.
   Pledges, approvals, signatures, payments and delivery stay distinct.
4. Coverage and comparability review before any outcome contrast. The screen
   may use already authorised, bounded source routes only; any new collection
   requires a named source, route, budget and stop condition.

No country, estimator, follow-up horizon, transformation or effect is selected
in advance. The source knowledge base remains authoritative; a derived snapshot
must be versioned and separate from canonical facts.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Frozen candidate-country and treatment-date records, completed before outcome comparison
- [ ] Validated country-quarter contract with source and missingness/denominator provenance
- [ ] Comparison admissibility assessment covering negotiation, concurrent interventions and spillovers
- [ ] Pre-specified falsifications, sensitivities and country-level uncertainty limits
- [ ] Evidence-backed GO, NARROW or DEFER, with exact failed conditions and next discriminating evidence if not GO
- [ ] No effect estimate, causal figure or descriptive substitution before a GO and separate author approval

